Applies the conductor-review skill's archive convention consistently to the registry
rather than only to the newest track.

The review skill's cleanup step is "Move to conductor/archive/ and remove from the
tracks file." The track archived in 9c32c5d kept a [x] registry entry instead,
matching the two older archived tracks, so the repository had a third convention
alongside the skill's. This settles it on the skill's reading: conductor/tracks.md
now lists active work only, and a finished track moves to conductor/archive/ and
leaves the file.

All three previously listed tracks were already in conductor/archive/, so the
registry is now just a header plus the convention itself, stated once so the next
track does not re-add a completed entry.

Removed: Async Intent Arbitration, Living Town Expansion, Resilient Progressive
Boot entries. None of the track content is lost - all 14 archive folders keep their
spec.md, plan.md, metadata.json, index.md, and the git notes that carry the
phase-by-phase verification.

Added "Track Archive" to conductor/index.md. Without it, stripping the registry
would have left conductor/archive/ unreachable from the Conductor index, since the
registry entries were the only thing pointing at it. All 8 links from index.md now
resolve. README.md already described conductor/archive/ as the home of finished
tracks, so that framing needed no change.

No source files touched, so no test run: this is two markdown files.
